Tom: Yes, I really want to. I love asking questions about how things work.
Lucy: Me too. What kind of project do you hope to do?
Tom: I''d like to study how clean water can stop disease.
Lucy: That sounds useful. I want to build a small telescope and look at the stars.
Tom: Wow, that''s a great idea. We could even share what we learn with the class.
Lucy: Exactly. The teacher says a real scientist always shares the results.
Tom: Then let''s sign up right now before the club is full!', '露西问汤姆今年是否要参加科学社团;汤姆很想参加,喜欢追问事物如何运作;他想研究干净的水如何阻止疾病;露西想做一架小望远镜看星星;两人打算把所学分享给全班,因为真正的科学家总会分享成果;于是决定趁名额没满赶紧报名。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Tom love doing?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Asking questions about how things work.","Playing computer games all day.","Selling old books.","Sleeping during class."]},{"q":"What project does Tom hope to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Build a fast car.","Study how clean water can stop disease.","Paint the classroom.","Write a song."]},{"q":"What does Lucy want to build?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A small telescope.","A new computer.","A water pump.","A toy boat."]},{"q":"Why do they want to share what they learn?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To win money.","Because a real scientist always shares the results.","To skip homework.","To make the teacher angry."]},{"q":"What do they decide to do at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Go home early.","Stop studying science.","Sign up before the club is full.","Wait until next year."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U1');
In fact, their work always begins with a question about the world.
They make a guess and then look for evidence to test it.
They take careful measurements and study the numbers.
Finally, they share their results so that everyone can benefit.', '许多人以为科学家只是在实验室里调配液体;其实他们的工作总是始于一个关于世界的问题;他们先做出猜想,再寻找证据去检验;他们仔细测量并研究数据;最后把成果分享出去,让所有人都能受益。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do many people wrongly think scientists do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Travel around the world.","Build houses.","Teach music.","Only mix liquids in a lab."]},{"q":"Where does a scientist''s work always begin?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["With a question about the world.","With a holiday.","With a finished answer.","With a new computer."]},{"q":"What do scientists look for after making a guess?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["More money.","Evidence to test it.","A quiet room.","A faster car."]},{"q":"What do they do with the numbers?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Throw them away.","Hide them.","Study them carefully.","Sell them."]},{"q":"Why do scientists share their results?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To keep them secret.","To make people afraid.","To waste time.","So that everyone can benefit."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U1');
Maria: Don''t worry. When data look contradictory, we simply test again.
David: But we''ve already run the experiment three times.
Maria: Then let''s calm down and check every measurement slowly.
David: You''re right. Maybe one of the numbers was written down wrong.
Maria: Exactly. A real scientist has to be patient and careful.
David: I see. So one strange result is not the end of the world.
Maria: No. It''s just a sign that we need to do some solid work.', '戴维说前两次结果完全不一致,感到沮丧;玛利亚说数据看似矛盾时,就再做一次;戴维说已经做了三次;玛利亚建议冷静下来逐项核对测量;戴维意识到可能有个数字记错了;玛利亚说真正的科学家必须耐心而细致;戴维明白一个奇怪的结果不是世界末日;玛利亚说那只是提醒他们要踏实工作。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does David feel frustrated?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The first two results don''t match.","He lost his notebook.","The lab is too cold.","He is hungry."]},{"q":"What does Maria suggest doing when data look contradictory?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Give up the project.","Test again.","Change the question.","Leave the lab."]},{"q":"How many times have they run the experiment?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Once.","Twice.","Three times.","Ten times."]},{"q":"What might explain the strange result?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The machine is new.","Maria was absent.","The room was dark.","One number was written down wrong."]},{"q":"What does Maria say a real scientist must be?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Patient and careful.","Loud and fast.","Rich and famous.","Quiet and shy."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U1');
He became famous while he was still a young student.
At a lecture, he stood up and found a mistake in the maths.
When the maths was corrected, the big bang theory was proven right.
Above all, he was brave and willing to admit his own faults.', '史蒂芬·霍金是一位研究宇宙的天才科学家;他在还是年轻学生时就出了名;在一场讲座上,他起身指出了数学计算中的一个错误;数学被改正后,大爆炸理论被证明是正确的;最重要的是,他勇敢且愿意承认自己的过错。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did Hawking study?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The ocean.","The universe.","Old languages.","Music."]},{"q":"When did he become famous?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["After he stopped working.","Only when he was very old.","While he was still a young student.","Before he went to school."]},{"q":"What did he do at the lecture?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["He fell asleep.","He left early.","He sang a song.","He found a mistake in the maths."]},{"q":"What was proven right after the maths was corrected?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The big bang theory.","The steady state theory.","Nothing at all.","An old idea."]},{"q":"What quality does the passage praise most?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He was very rich.","He was willing to admit his faults.","He was very lucky.","He never made mistakes."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U1');
Mr Lee: Start with a clear question that you really want to answer.
Anna: All right. What should I do after that?
Mr Lee: Make a guess, and then collect evidence to test it.
Anna: How do I know if my result is trustworthy?
Mr Lee: Repeat the test, and ask a friend to repeat it too.
Anna: That makes sense. So one result is never enough.
Mr Lee: Right. And remember to share what you find with others.', '安娜想做一个小研究项目却不知如何开始;李老师建议先提出一个真正想回答的清晰问题;然后做出猜想并收集证据去检验;安娜问如何判断结果是否可信;李老师说要重复实验,并请同学也重复一次;安娜明白一个结果远远不够;李老师叮嘱她要把发现分享给别人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Anna''s problem?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She has no friends.","She is afraid of the dark.","She doesn''t know how to begin her project.","She lost her books."]},{"q":"What does Mr Lee say to start with?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A long holiday.","A finished report.","A new computer.","A clear question she wants to answer."]},{"q":"What should Anna do after making a guess?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Collect evidence to test it.","Forget about it.","Sell the idea.","Wait a year."]},{"q":"How can Anna check if her result is trustworthy?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Change the question.","Repeat it and ask a friend to repeat it too.","Stop the test.","Only trust herself."]},{"q":"What does Mr Lee remind her to do at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Keep it secret.","Throw away her data.","Share what she finds with others.","Give up the project."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U1');
Never be afraid to ask a question, even a strange one.
Every great discovery once began as a single curious question.
If your first idea is wrong, try again with fresh eyes.
A curious mind today can change the world tomorrow.', '给每一个热爱科学的年轻人一个小贴士:永远不要害怕提问,哪怕是个奇怪的问题;每一项伟大的发现都曾始于一个好奇的问题;如果第一个想法错了,就换个角度重新尝试;今天一颗好奇的心,明天能改变世界。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only old professors.","Only teachers.","Only doctors.","Any young person who loves science."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say about asking questions?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Never be afraid to ask, even a strange one.","Never ask anything.","Only ask easy ones.","Ask only your teacher."]},{"q":"How did every great discovery once begin?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["With a lot of money.","As a single curious question.","With a finished answer.","By accident only."]},{"q":"What should you do if your first idea is wrong?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Stop forever.","Blame others.","Try again with fresh eyes.","Hide the mistake."]},{"q":"What can a curious mind do tomorrow?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Waste time.","Make people angry.","Lose its way.","Change the world."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U1');

